 tutional-courts-times-crisis-mexican-experience
CATEGORIES:Law,Politics
DESCRIPTION:Faculty of Law\nHighlight: Senior figure speaking (Justice of t
 he Supreme Court)\nTopics: Law\, Politics\nDetails: https://www.law.cam.ac
 .uk/events/dialogues-democratic-resilience-constitutional-courts-times-cri
 sis-mexican-experience\nSign-up needed: https://cam-ac-uk.zoom.us/webinar/
 register/WN_C3zFlTtARXqRjWSJ8Cm5BQ#/registration\nAlfredo Gutiérrez Ortiz
  Mena (Former Justice of the Supreme Court of Mexico and former Henry J. S
 teiner Lecturer in Human Rights at Harvard Law School)\n\n Date/time: \n\n
  Monday 23 November 2026 \n\n 5:00pm to 6:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Online w
 ebinar\n\n Sign up\n\n About \n\n About the series: the Dialogues on Democ
 ratic Resilience series provides a platform for scholars\, students\, and 
 members of the general public to examine the causes and dynamics of democr
 atic decline and to explore strategies for strengthening democratic instit
 utions. Interdisciplinary in scope\, the series places particular emphasis
  on the role of law and legal institutions\, investigating how they can bo
 th contribute to democratic erosion and function as vital safeguards again
 st.\n For questions\, please contact Dr Raffael Fasel ( rnf22@cam.ac.uk )
END:VEVENT
